s. Garam masala is used in a wide range of dishes, including marinades, pickles, stews, and curries."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-garam-masala"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garam_masala"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Indian cuisine","cuisine/indian-cuisine",[["Baingan bharta","dish/baingan-bharta"],["Butter chicken","dish/butter-chicken"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Brinjal","ingredient/brinjal"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Cilantro","ingredient/cilantro"],["Coriander","ingredient/coriander"],["Cumin","ingredient/cumin"],["Green peas","ingredient/green-peas"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Kasuri methi","ingredient/kasuri-methi"],["Tomatoes","ingredient/tomatoes"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/5/58/Garammasalaphoto.jpg/500px-Garammasalaphoto.jpg","w":500,"h":373,"by":"Badagnani","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Garammasalaphoto.jpg"}},"ingredient/bean":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/bean","n":"Bean","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 6 dishes across 7 cuisines","intro":[["A bean is the seed of plants in many genera of the legume family (Fabaceae) used as a vegetable for human consumption or animal feed. The seeds are sold fresh or preserved through drying (a pulse). Beans have been cultivated since the seventh millennium BCE in Thailand, and since the second millennium BCE in Europe and in Peru. Most beans, with the exception of peas, are summer crops. As legumes, the plants fix nitrogen and form seeds with a high protein content. They are produced on a scale of millions of tons annually in many countries, with India as the largest producer."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-bean"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bean"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":7,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Brunswick stew","dish/brunswick-stew"],["Chimichanga","dish/chimichanga"]]],["Georgian cuisine","cuisine/georgian-cuisine",[["Lobiani","dish/lobiani"]]],["German cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine",[["Eintopf","dish/eintopf"]]],["Mexican cuisine","cuisine/mexican-cuisine",[["Chimichanga","dish/chimichanga"]]],["Serbian cuisine","cuisine/serbian-cuisine",[["Pasulj","dish/pasulj"]]],["Thuringian cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine-thuringia",[["Eintopf","dish/eintopf"]]],["Turkish cuisine","cuisine/turkish-cuisine",[["Piyaz","dish/piyaz"]]]]},{"h":"Where it's grown","grown":{"what":"Beans, dry","years":"2020 to 2024","url":"https://www.fao.org/faostat/en/#data/QCL","world":29765208,"top":[["India","cuisine/indian-cuisine",7880613],["Brazil","cuisine/brazilian-cuisine",2945451],["Myanmar","cuisine/burmese-cuisine",2629516],["Tanzania","cuisine/tanzanian-cuisine",1355270],["China","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",1322710],["United States of America","cuisine/american-cuisine",1222307],["Mexico","cuisine/mexican-cuisine",1006057],["Kenya","cuisine/kenyan-cuisine",791645],["Uganda","cuisine/ugandan-cuisine",788425],["Ethiopia","cuisine/ethiopian-cuisine",784771],["Argentina","cuisine/argentine-cuisine",667929],["Burundi","cuisine/burundian-cuisine",492940],["Mozambique","cuisine/mozambican-cuisine",477889],["Rwanda","cuisine/rwandan-cuisine",461773],["Canada","cuisine/canadian-cuisine",385905]]}},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Phaseolus","ingredient/phaseolus"],["Game meat","ingredient/game-meat"],["Maize","ingredient/maize"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Adobada","ingredient/adobada"],["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Flour tortilla","ingredient/flour-tortilla"],["Jalapeño","ingredient/jalapeno"],["Machaca","ingredient/machaca"],["Rice","i