ubbing snack on a par with pizza.\""]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-koni-store"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koni_Store"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Just One Cookbook","ref":"site/justonecookbook-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"justonecookbook.com","note":"Namiko Chen's long-running blog and videos on Japanese home cooking.","url":"https://justonecookbook.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"RecipeTin Japan","ref":"site/japan-recipetineats-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"japan.recipetineats.com","note":"Japanese home recipes from Yumiko, a Japan-born cook, sister site to RecipeTin Eats.","url":"https://japan.recipetineats.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Japanese cuisine","links":[["Benihana","dish/benihana"],["Bergh–Stoutenburgh House","dish/bergh-stoutenburgh-house"],["Bincho","dish/bincho"],["Boxer Ramen","dish/boxer-ramen"],["Cagen","dish/cagen"],["Chikuwa","dish/chikuwa"],["Curry bread","dish/curry-bread"],["Donburi","dish/donburi"],["Em (restaurant)","dish/em-restaurant"],["Esaki (restaurant)","dish/esaki-restaurant"],["Feng Sushi","dish/feng-sushi"],["Freshness Burger","dish/freshness-burger"],["Fukamushicha","dish/fukamushicha"],["Gyokuro","dish/gyokuro"],["Heihachi Jaya","dish/heihachi-jaya"],["Hitsumabushi","dish/hitsumabushi"],["HokBen","dish/hokben"],["Hokka Hokka Tei","dish/hokka-hokka-tei"],["Horumonyaki","dish/horumonyaki"],["Ichibanya","dish/ichibanya"],["Ichigo Ichie","dish/ichigo-ichie"],["Ichimura at Brushstroke","dish/ichimura-at-brushstroke"],["Iekei ramen","dish/iekei-ramen"],["Inago no tsukudani","dish/inago-no-tsukudani"],["Ishikawa (restaurant)","dish/ishikawa-restaurant"],["Italian Tomato","dish/italian-tomato"],["Itamae","dish/itamae"],["Itsu","dish/itsu"],["Ivan Ramen","dish/ivan-ramen"],["Izakaya","dish/izakaya"],["Izumi (restaurant)","dish/izumi-restaurant"],["Japanese cheesecake","dish/japanese-cheesecake"],["Japanese noodles","dish/japanese-noodles"],["Japanese restaurant","dish/japanese-restaurant"],["Japanese tea","dish/japanese-tea"],["Jingisukan","dish/jingisukan"],["Jinya Ramen Bar","dish/jinya-ramen-bar"],["Kadowaki (restaurant)","dish/kadowaki-restaurant"],["Kaki furai","dish/kaki-furai"],["Kamaboko","dish/kamaboko"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/a/ac/Koni_Store_-_Botafogo_Praia_Shopping.jpg/500px-Koni_Store_-_Botafogo_Praia_Shopping.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Eduardo P","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Koni_Store_-_Botafogo_Praia_Shopping.jpg"}},"ingredient/silver-stripe-round-herring":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/silver-stripe-round-herring","n":"Silver-stripe round herring","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["The silver-stripe round herring, slender sprat, or Kibinago minnow (Spratelloides gracilis) is a small, herring-like forage fish. They are small fish used as fishing bait, especially in skipjack tuna-fishing. It is valued as food in Japan, where it is known as kibinago. These can be eaten raw, as sashimi, or cooked, as whitebait."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-silver-stripe-round-herring"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver-stripe_round_herring"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Malay cuisine","cuisine/malay-cuisine",[["Lekor","dish/lekor"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Fish","ingredient/fish"],["Rastrelliger kanagurta","ingredient/rastrelliger-kanagurta"],["Round sardinella","ingredient/round-sardinella"],["Sago","ingredient/sago"],["Tapioca starch","ingredient/tapioca-starch"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/8/8c/XRF-Spratelloides_gracilis.jpg/500px-XRF-Spratelloides_gracilis.jpg","w":500,"h":248,"by":"Xavier Romero-Frias","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:XRF-Spratelloides_gracilis.jpg"}},"dish/mianwo":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/mianwo","n":"Mianwo","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Mianwo is a deep-fried, donut-shaped snack from Wuhan in Hubei province in central China. It is made from soy milk, rice milk, flour, sesame, and chopped Chinese scallion. Mianwo usually has a salty taste, but a sweeter variant may be made with diced sweet potato."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-mianwo"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mianwo"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"],["Hubei cuisine","cuisine/hubei-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Allium fistulosum","ingredient/allium-fistulosum"],["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Sesame","ingredient/sesame"],["Soybean","ingredient/soybean"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Woks of Life","ref":"site/thewoksoflife-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"thewoksoflife.com","note":"Chinese and Chinese American recipes from the Leung family, running since 2013.","url":"https://thewoksoflife.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Chinese Cooking Demystified","ref":"site/youtube-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"youtube.com","note":"Technique-heavy YouTube channel on regional Chinese home and restaurant cooking.","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@ChineseCookingDemystified","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"},{"name":"Red House Spice","ref":"site/redhousespice-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"redhousespice.com","note":"Classic Chinese recipes from Wei Guo, who grew up in Gansu, blogging since 2017.","url":"https://redhousespice.com/about/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Madame Hu